From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Darren Shepherd <darren@obot.ai>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 23:39:53 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] input: clear_selection binding action

There was no way to clear a selection except to imitate one: Windows
Terminal's control sent a press and a release with no movement, because that
is what collapses a selection in ghostty's own mouse handling. Behaviour by
imitation, and it would have broken silently if that handling changed.

The action ends the click gesture along with the selection, and that is part
of the action rather than a side effect. A selection cleared while the button
is still held is recreated by the very next pointer movement, and the click
count left behind makes the next press a double click. mouseButtonCallback
already pairs the two the same way when mouse reporting takes over mid-press.

Ending the gesture is also what lets an embedder that computes its own
selection anchors re-press where it means to: ghostty latches the anchor on a
press and will not re-latch, and a second press within a cell of the first is
a double click.

zig build test: 3091 passed, 58 skipped, 0 failed.

Verified end to end in harness/hwnd-host (GHOSTTY_HARNESS_CLEAR_SELECTION):
a drag selects, the action clears it, and an immediate re-press at the same
pixel yields a fresh two-character selection. Mutation-checked - with the
gesture reset removed, that re-press comes back as the whole word.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BgDGqEqRBB8L5Ueoq1uuxy
---
 src/Surface.zig       | 14 ++++++++++++++
 src/input/Binding.zig | 10 ++++++++++
 src/input/command.zig |  6 ++++++
 3 files changed, 30 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/Surface.zig b/src/Surface.zig
index 4e6bd96eb..32d20d289 100644
--- a/src/Surface.zig
+++ b/src/Surface.zig
@@ -5524,6 +5524,20 @@ pub fn performBindingAction(self: *Surface, action: input.Binding.Action) !bool
             }
         },
 
+        .clear_selection => {
+            self.renderer_state.mutex.lockUncancelable(global.io());
+            defer self.renderer_state.mutex.unlock(global.io());
+
+            // The gesture goes with the selection. A selection cleared while
+            // the button is still held would be recreated by the very next
+            // pointer movement, and the click count left behind would make the
+            // next press a double click. This is the same pairing mouseButtonCallback
+            // does when mouse reporting takes over mid-press.
+            try self.setSelection(null);
+            self.mouse.selection_gesture.reset(self.renderer_state.terminal);
+            try self.queueRender();
+        },
+
         .inspector => |mode| return try self.rt_app.performAction(
             .{ .surface = self },
             .inspector,
diff --git a/src/input/Binding.zig b/src/input/Binding.zig
index 8c706027a..ef5843470 100644
--- a/src/input/Binding.zig
+++ b/src/input/Binding.zig
@@ -438,6 +438,15 @@ pub const Action = union(enum) {
     /// Select all text on the screen.
     select_all,
 
+    /// Clear the current selection, if there is one, and end any click or
+    /// drag gesture in progress.
+    ///
+    /// Ending the gesture is part of the action rather than a side effect of
+    /// it: a selection cleared while the button is still held would be
+    /// recreated by the very next pointer movement, and the click count left
+    /// behind would make the next press a double click.
+    clear_selection,
+
     /// Scroll to the top of the screen.
     scroll_to_top,
 
@@ -1374,6 +1383,7 @@ pub const Action = union(enum) {
             .set_tab_title,
             .clear_screen,
             .select_all,
+            .clear_selection,
             .scroll_to_top,
             .scroll_to_bottom,
             .scroll_to_selection,
diff --git a/src/input/command.zig b/src/input/command.zig
index ac048eec0..ea7288ab8 100644
--- a/src/input/command.zig
+++ b/src/input/command.zig
@@ -241,6 +241,12 @@ fn actionCommands(action: Action.Key) []const Command {
             .description = "Select all text on the screen.",
         }},
 
+        .clear_selection => comptime &.{.{
+            .action = .clear_selection,
+            .title = "Clear Selection",
+            .description = "Clear the current selection.",
+        }},
+
         .scroll_to_top => comptime &.{.{
             .action = .scroll_to_top,
             .title = "Scroll to Top",
